WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
Warm a coil of metal wire in a water bath.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.310
Its resistance creeps up.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.770
Swap in a thermistor and do the same.

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:12.200
Its resistance drops, steeply
at first, then less steeply.

5
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.130
Same water.

6
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.330
Same heating.

7
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.270
The opposite result.

8
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.910
Why does warming push these two
resistances in opposite directions?

9
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.030
In this mission, you'll meet the diode,
a component that lets current through

10
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.080
in one direction only.

11
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.020
Then you'll read the thermistor's graphs,

12
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.970
and see why it makes a
good temperature sensor.

13
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:37.330
Your mission: explain why heating changes
the two resistances in opposite ways.
